.TH NN-OPS 1 "2026" "nn 0.1.0" "NN Manual"
.SH NAME
nn-ops \- list operators in a model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nn ops [options] <model>
.SH DESCRIPTION
List operators, optionally grouped or filtered.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-by\-type
Group by operator type.
.TP
.B \-\-by\-cost
Sort by compute cost.
.TP
.B \-\-by\-memory
Sort by memory.
.TP
.B \-\-details
Per-node details.
.TP
.B \-\-unsupported
List unknown/unrecognized ops.
.TP
.B \-\-canonical
Use canonical names.
.TP
.B \-\-native
Use native names.
.TP
.B \-\-op TYPE
Filter by operator type.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nn ops model.onnx
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
nn-inspect(1), nn-compute(1)
